  "description": "The project-pinned sealed-packet composition (NOT libsodium crypto_box_seal): per-packet ephemeral X25519; shared = X25519(esk, rpk), abort on all-zero; key = BLAKE2b-256('111/seal/v1' || shared || epk || rpk); nonce = BLAKE2b-192('111/seal-n/v1' || epk || rpk) (derived, never transmitted); XChaCha20-Poly1305 over (sender_node_id(32) || plaintext) with AD = the exact cleartext header bytes (version || crypto_mode || counter(LE u64) || extra_len || extra); packet = header || epk(32) || ciphertext||tag(16). The KAT pins esk to RFC 7748 Alice's scalar so the packet is deterministic; the conformance suite re-computes it with an independent in-test model of the section 6.4 recipe AND opens it through the public seal::open. 'expect' tokens (open): ok | err:truncated | err:mode:<b> | err:ecdh:<EcdhError> | err:auth | err:short-plaintext. Counters are decimal strings (u64).",
